From 98499ef525ab824c91fc8d92c4fe2d292e431e4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:23:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] turnip (Doris): no LRZ for Eden

In a stock Eden, Apex Doris 9 (render mode measured per pass, mostly SYSMEM) has no distant flicker in
Tears of the Kingdom but square blocks of the ground turn black and flicker; every pass in GMEM (Apex's
TOTK rule) hides them but is slow and makes distant objects flicker. LRZ culls in blocks and is the
suspect, and Apex's own TOTK rule also touched an LRZ option. For the engine "yuzu Emulator", turn LRZ
off as TU_DEBUG=nolrz does; per-pixel depth testing is unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
index b554a5b024c..c6cfd21c137 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -3220,6 +3220,17 @@ tu_CreateDevice(VkPhysicalDevice physicalDevice,
       (!border_color_without_format ||
        !physical_device->instance->drirc.misc.enable_d24s8_border_color_workaround);
    device->use_lrz = !TU_DEBUG_START(NOLRZ);
+   {
+      /* Eden (Doris): no LRZ (the coarse block depth cull) for Eden, the same as TU_DEBUG=nolrz. In Tears
+       * of the Kingdom, with most render passes drawn straight to memory (SYSMEM), square blocks of the
+       * ground turn black and flicker; drawing everything in tile memory hides them but is slow and makes
+       * distant objects flicker. LRZ culls in blocks and is the suspect. Per-pixel depth testing is
+       * unaffected.
+       */
+      const char *engine = physical_device->instance->vk.app_info.engine_name;
+      if (engine && !strcmp(engine, "yuzu Emulator"))
+         device->use_lrz = false;
+   }
 
    tu_gpu_tracepoint_config_variable();
 
